# Compile ratstack.sh documents with plain Svelte

## Decision

Use Svelte as a build-time document compiler, not as the Worker runtime.

`apps/mischief/scripts/generate-content.ts` reads checked-in Markdown and MDSvX through Effect `FileSystem`, compiles the content through mdsvex's unified pipeline, renders it with Svelte's server renderer, and atomically writes the generated TypeScript module. `apps/mischief/src/document.svelte` is the shared semantic document shell.

The Cloudflare Worker still owns routing, content negotiation, caching, MCP, HTTP capabilities, rate limits, and the sandbox. There is no SvelteKit adapter, router, hydration step, browser bundle, or client-side application code.

## Representations

- The default response remains the exact checked-in Markdown or MDSvX source with `text/markdown`.
- Requests that accept `text/html` receive the generated Svelte document.
- HTML and source use separate static cache representations and ETags.
- The build fails if a generated application document contains a `<script>` element. Cloudflare may still add its analytics beacon after the Worker response.

## Effect boundary

Effect owns build I/O, typed `ContentBuildError` failures, concurrent source reads and compilation, package JSON decoding, and the final atomic write. Pure hashing, slugging, AST traversal, and string assembly remain ordinary functions.

## Document shell (2026-09-22)

`apps/mischief/src/document.svelte` is a man page, not a marketing site. Monospace everywhere so box-drawing diagrams line up, an 80ch measure, light only (Joel rejected dark mode: no `prefers-color-scheme`, no `background`, no colour variables), default link colours, and `<hr>` rules above and below the nav. There is no logo in the header; `🐀 Rat Stack` is the single h1 on the home page and a small link back home elsewhere. `assets/ratstack-logo.svg` is still read at build time only to serve `/favicon.svg`; nothing else is fetched.

Tables stack on phones. A build-time rehype plugin writes each cell's column header into `data-label`, and under 40rem the CSS hides `thead`, turns rows and cells into blocks, and prints the label before each value.

Diagrams follow the `show-me` skill: one fenced `text` block, Unicode box drawing, under 80 columns, followed by a `What to notice` line. The same block ships in the Markdown representation, so agents and browsers see one diagram. Quiver (Arrow) drew the logo and stays available for marks and Open Graph art, not for diagrams, because an SVG would exist only in the HTML face.

Table cells reset `overflow-wrap` to `normal`; the page-level `anywhere` setting shredded words into single characters on phones.

## Wiki links, backlinks, and a change log (2026-09-22)

After Karpathy's LLM Wiki gist: the site is a compiled, cross-referenced wiki over the repo, not a pile of pages. `generate-content.ts` now does three things at build time.

- **Cross-references.** A `rehype` plugin (`linkCodeSpans`) turns inline code spans into links when the span names a served page (`AGENTS.md`, a skill name) or a real repository path (`packages/core/src/inspect-file.ts`). Served pages link inside the site; repo paths link to GitHub `blob` or `tree` on `main`. Every path is checked on disk with Effect `FileSystem.exists`/`stat`, so the build cannot mint a dead link; placeholders like `<capability>.ts` and `node_modules/...` stay plain. Fenced blocks and existing links are skipped, and a page never links to itself.
- **Provenance and backlinks.** Each HTML page ends with `Last changed <date> in <commit>`, a GitHub source link, and `Linked from: ...` listing the in-site pages that reference it. `ChildProcessSpawner` from `effect/unstable/process` runs `git log -1` per source concurrently.
- **`/log.md`.** A generated change log, newest first, of every commit that touched a served file, linking each entry to its commit. It sits beside `pins.md` as a second generated law resource.

- **Entities.** The stack pieces (Effect, XState, TypeScript 7, Oxlint, Oxfmt, Vitest, lefthook, pnpm, Turborepo, Alchemy, Cloudflare Workers, MCP, OpenAPI) are wiki entities: `linkStackEntities` links the first plain-text mention on each page to the tool's home, skipping headings, code, and existing links. Longer names win (`Effect diagnostics` before `Effect`). All URLs answered 200 on 2026-09-22.

Cache lesson from the same day: the edge cache key is `staticContentVersion`, and it used to digest only inputs and Worker source. A compiler-only deploy (the entity plugin) kept the old key and Cloudflare served the previous HTML with `x-ratstack-cache: HIT`. The digest now includes every rendered document, so any change to the output changes the key.

These additions live only in the HTML representation. The Markdown representation stays the exact checked-in source so digests and agent reads do not change.

## Compatibility rules

- Preserve the previous heading slug algorithm so existing anchors do not move.
- Keep the responsive shell minimal: mobile gutters, wrapping navigation, and contained `pre` and table overflow.
- Treat checked-in documents as trusted compiler input. Revisit sanitization if the source boundary widens.
- Use unique temporary files because Turborepo may run `generate`, `typecheck`, and `build` concurrently.

## Evidence

- `pnpm turbo run check test build --force`: 20/20 tasks passed.
- Mischief tests: 14/14 passed, including exact source, negotiated HTML, frontmatter removal, tables, stable headings, caching, no application scripts, GitHub and in-site code-span links, backlinks, last-changed provenance, and `/log.md`.
- `pnpm mischief:smoke`: production remained 5/5 Agent-Native.
- Production returned formatted HTML for both public `.svx` resources and exact source for default requests.
- A 390px browser check reported a 390px document width and a 358px contained table.
